Some of my favourite ideas for intersting levels:-

* Fun fair/ Carnival layer with different sorts of mirrors in them -

on looking in the mirror "You seem rather thin" (you also lose hitpoints
or food...) 
			 "You are looking good" (+ on Charisma)
			 "You look displaced" (moves you 1 randomly)
			 "Gosh! You do look tired" (sleep 1-10)
			 "My! Did even your mother love you?" (- Charisma)
			 "What big muscles you have" (+ strength)
			 etc
I was thinking of these being mirrors on walls but perhaps these are 
simply the random results of using a magic mirror.

Lots of monsters on this level that try to scare you but if you are
not scared will tend to run away themselves.

THe clowns will throw cream pies and generally be a nuisance though they
are of course peaceful....

* A layer full of holy places/oracles/shops - this is where tourists
go if they go to heaven.... its called the Holy City... The kops are
roaming free so watch out...

* Hypermarket - lots of shops

* Smugglers cave - lots of piratical goodies like gold, chests, jewels
and of course potions of rum, maybe even a fountain or sink that serves
up only rum - jolly useful if you need confusing.  A new tool called an
eye-patch will allow you to pass yourself off as a pirate - the full
costume worn by the (human) pirates would include gold earrings, pirate
hats or scarves, crutches, scimatars, daggers, jewels set in their
teeth.  And of course some of them keep pet parrots.

* A chain of islands with ferries between. Its cheap to go out but
the return journey is much more expensive (unless you bought a return.)
Each island is home to a different colony of creatures/fabulous beast/
human settlement/barren wasteland.

